      <div type="commentary">
        <p n="1">The framed manuscript page number ⲓⲋ stands at the left on this page and is printed with a bar above and below as the frame, not as a supralinear stroke.</p>
        <p n="1">The stroke of ϩⲛ̄ (measured 644–656) is short and sits over the gap between ϩ and ⲛ, covering 35 % of ⲛ and 15 % of ϩ; it is assigned to ⲛ, the letter it covers more.</p>
        <p n="6">The edition prints a closing bracket after ϫ with no opening bracket; the three dots before it are therefore encoded as illegible.</p>
        <p n="11">Lines 11–13: the editors print "nicht gelesen" (not read) at the start of the line; it is kept as a transcriber note.</p>
        <p n="15">Measured strokes: the first (1083–1100) covers ⲛ 50 % and ϥ 53 % and is encoded as one stroke over both; a second separate stroke stands over ⲣ.</p>
        <p n="16">Lines 16–17: the editors print "verwischt und abgerieben" (smeared and rubbed off) at the start of the line; it is kept as a transcriber note.</p>
        <p n="18">The editors print "verwischt" (smeared) followed by a wide blank before ⲛ; both are kept as one transcriber note.</p>
        <p n="20">The editors print "verwischt" (smeared) between the dots. For the beginning they suggest roughly [ⲛⲧⲙⲛⲧⲛⲁϭ ⲁⲡⲉⲧⲁϥ]ϣⲱⲡⲉ or similar (apparatus).</p>
        <p n="30">Measured overline 477–536: it covers ⲡⲣⲕ and not ⲗ (19 %) or ⲥ.</p>
        <p n="33">The chapter numeral ⲃ̄ is printed on both sides of the two title lines, centred between them, close to the title rather than in the outer margins.</p>
        <p n="35">The edition prints [ϥ ⲁⲧ(ⲣ)ⲉϥϩⲉⲣ]: the ⲣ stands in parentheses inside the restoration. The parentheses cannot be encoded; the restoration is recorded as [ϥ ⲁⲧⲣⲉϥϩⲉⲣ].</p>
      </div>
